Subject: [PATCH 040/154] feat: delete traffic routing, whose answer only Swift
 had
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every route decision came from UIBridge::CopyRouteForURL, so all three hooks
have declined on their first line since the cut. The feature and its later
fix have both been dead for a day.

Gone: MaybeRerouteNavigation (chrome::Navigate), MaybeRerouteNewContents
(window.open), MaybeRerouteRendererNavigation and the throttle that called
it, both upstream call sites, the throttle registration, and the friend
declarations that let a reroute reach BrowserController's private surface.

ScopedRoutingBypass goes with them, and this corrects my own note on the
task. NewTabWithURL does construct one at every AddTabAt, but g_routing_bypass
had no reader outside the three hooks, so it set a value nobody read. The
loop-prevention contract it carried is recorded for the follow-up.

Kept, with its gtest suite: atrium_routing_navigation_decision. It is the
pure eligibility rule - main frame, renderer-initiated, not same-document,
user gesture, link transition, http or https, no bypass, resolvable
non-little controller - and the only place that rule is written down. The
rebuild starts from it rather than from a re-reading of the throttle.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
